WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.150
The best part of any impact report is the
people in it.

2
00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:07.684
Storyraise Collect gathers their stories,
and your reports tell them.

3
00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:11.562
Start a new collection and choose what you
want to collect, like thank-yous from the

4
00:00:11.572 --> 00:00:14.355
students your donors support.

5
00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.270
Add the fields you need:

6
00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:21.431
short text for a name, long text for their
story, and a file upload for a photo.

7
00:00:21.644 --> 00:00:26.063
Each field saves to a variable, like
student note.

8
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.392
Get form link and send it however you
like.

9
00:00:29.402 --> 00:00:32.766
Students answer on any device, photo and
all.

10
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:37.443
Every answer lands in the collection, one
row per student, ready to review, edit, or

11
00:00:37.453 --> 00:00:38.912
export.

12
00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.378
In your report, add a repeater.

13
00:00:41.893 --> 00:00:45.667
Under Repeat For Each Item in, select your
collection.

14
00:00:45.677 --> 00:00:49.754
Then lay out one story card with variables
like student name, and set its image to

15
00:00:49.764 --> 00:00:51.792
the student's photo.

16
00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:54.123
Now tell it which stories to show.

17
00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:58.384
Under Repeat When, match the fund code
each student entered to the fund reference

18
00:00:58.394 --> 00:01:00.137
on every donor's record.

19
00:01:00.147 --> 00:01:03.539
Each donor sees the students their own
gift supports.

20
00:01:03.549 --> 00:01:07.324
Emily Wilson's fund supports Sophia and
David, so theirs are the stories she

21
00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:08.363
reads.

22
00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.196
James Taylor sees Grace and Marcus
instead.

23
00:01:11.293 --> 00:01:16.671
And when a new matching story comes in, it
shows up the next time the report opens.

24
00:01:16.681 --> 00:01:20.300
Collect the stories once, and every report
tells the right ones.
